WEBVTT

00:02.630 --> 00:03.880
The Big Four.

00:04.250 --> 00:10.970
It is the title of Tempest's strongest executives
chosen to protect Great Demon Lord Rimuru!

00:20.480 --> 00:22.980
To join Benimaru, Shion, and Diablo

00:23.060 --> 00:25.440
as the last member of the Big Four,

00:25.530 --> 00:28.900
the strong who has passed the preliminary
rounds have gathered here today!

00:29.240 --> 00:30.490
However!

00:30.570 --> 00:34.700
There were also those who participated
to take down Demon Lord Rimuru!

00:34.950 --> 00:38.000
Will the winner earn the title
of the Big Four?

00:38.080 --> 00:41.170
Or will they take Demon Lord
Rimuru's head as their reward?

00:41.670 --> 00:46.460
We will now begin the main matches
of Tempest Battle Tournament!

00:50.340 --> 00:52.260
The Big Four, eh…

02:23.560 --> 02:23.850
(Episode 69: The Battle Tournament)

02:23.940 --> 02:26.560
(Episode 69: The Battle Tournament)
We're not allowed to enter the battle tournament?!

02:26.650 --> 02:28.360
(Episode 69: The Battle Tournament)
Why, Great Rimuru?!

02:28.520 --> 02:31.820
<i>Because you guys</i>
<i>will win if you did.</i>

02:32.240 --> 02:33.610
Uhh…

02:33.700 --> 02:37.990
Actually, you three are exceptionally
strong among my subordinates.

02:38.070 --> 02:42.660
So I was thinking of appointing you three
to new posts under the name "Big Four."

02:42.750 --> 02:44.210
Big Four?

02:44.290 --> 02:46.750
What a delightful sound.

02:46.960 --> 02:50.500
But I'm still unsure on who
should I pick for the last spot.

02:51.210 --> 02:56.630
So I'm planning to give the post to the one who
can expose the Hero Masayuki's true strength

02:56.720 --> 03:00.180
and win the Battle Tournament.

03:00.680 --> 03:02.020
I see!

03:02.100 --> 03:03.980
That makes sense!

03:06.100 --> 03:10.270
<i>I only came out with the title on</i>
<i>the fly to stop them from competing…</i>

03:10.520 --> 03:12.730
<i>But it became quite a big deal now.</i>

03:13.280 --> 03:17.860
My name is Soka.
I'll be your host for today!

03:18.870 --> 03:23.490
Now, let me introduce you all to our six
competitors who won the preliminary rounds!

03:26.460 --> 03:30.340
First, our most popular competitor!

03:30.500 --> 03:35.590
The young Hero, Masayuki!

03:40.640 --> 03:41.800
What's that?!

03:41.890 --> 03:43.720
There are picture on the sky!

03:44.720 --> 03:46.480
A light magic, eh?

03:46.730 --> 03:48.390
What a way to use it.

03:53.360 --> 03:56.030
No one has ever seen his
graceful sword skills before.

03:56.110 --> 04:01.070
Why? Because the moment he takes out
his blade, his opponent is already dead!

04:01.240 --> 04:04.160
Masayuki!

04:04.240 --> 04:08.500
Anyone who can see his gallant figure
should consider themselves lucky!

04:09.620 --> 04:12.130
"No one has ever seen
his sword skills before"?

04:12.210 --> 04:15.380
Then how on earth
did he win his way up?

04:15.800 --> 04:20.680
To be honest, I wasn't able to gauge
his strength from yesterday's matches.

04:20.760 --> 04:21.470
Huh?

04:21.550 --> 04:25.010
Next is Jinrai,
a battle-hardened warrior!

04:25.100 --> 04:29.270
Known as the Mad Wolf,
he's the Hero Masayuki's right-hand man!

04:29.440 --> 04:30.480
Because of him.

04:30.940 --> 04:33.270
He's one of Hero Masayuki's fellow.

04:33.360 --> 04:37.780
He took down all other qualifiers
and gave the Hero the win.

04:38.440 --> 04:42.870
Because of him, Masayuki was able to win
his way without even pulling his sword.

04:43.490 --> 04:47.370
So the Hero's power is still a mystery, huh.

04:47.870 --> 04:51.000
Our third competitor is
Gaiye the Flowing Swordsman!

04:51.080 --> 04:56.380
He dances like a seasoned performer during
battle, stealing the hearts of all who watch!

04:57.170 --> 05:00.430
Our fourth competitor is
the head of the Boyoids, Boyix!

05:00.510 --> 05:05.810
And the fifth competitor is Boyix's eternal
rival, the head of the Equinoids, Equix!

05:06.100 --> 05:10.940
Aren't they the guys I named because I
want them to serve as dungeon bosses?

05:11.020 --> 05:11.940
Yes, sir.

05:12.020 --> 05:14.940
Apparently they want
to be one of the Big Four,

05:15.020 --> 05:18.780
so they took down all the other monsters
in the preliminary rounds.

05:19.110 --> 05:21.400
Either one of these two
will serve as one of

05:21.490 --> 05:24.240
the masters of the dungeon
scheduled to open tomorrow!

05:24.320 --> 05:26.080
If you feel worthy of the challenge,

05:26.160 --> 05:30.830
summon your courage and plunge into
the dungeon in search of fame and fortune!

05:30.910 --> 05:33.370
She advertised the dungeon and everything!

05:33.460 --> 05:35.630
Good job, Soka.

05:36.380 --> 05:43.090
Moving on, we have a mysterious masked man
who showed tremendous strength yesterday!

05:43.550 --> 05:46.760
Is he a defender of justice
or a servant of evil?!

05:46.850 --> 05:51.890
Lion Mask!

05:53.310 --> 05:55.310
S-Soei, isn't that…

05:55.400 --> 05:58.270
Yes, without a doubt. It's <i>him</i>.

05:58.520 --> 06:02.150
Oh, here we have a message
from an anonymous individual.

06:02.490 --> 06:05.910
"Lion Mask, you better
do your best in my place!"

06:05.990 --> 06:09.790
"I know you know this, but don't let anyone
discover your identity, no matter what!"

06:10.160 --> 06:12.410
"Good luck!"

06:12.750 --> 06:14.170
So it says.

06:15.500 --> 06:20.170
<i>That's Milim, all right. She sent</i>
<i>in her own subordinate as her rep.</i>

06:20.380 --> 06:24.800
Now I've introduced all six of our competitors,
all left is two special entries!

06:25.090 --> 06:29.560
Here comes the strong, said to be
the closest to be part of the Big Four!

06:29.890 --> 06:35.020
First is our young warrior captain, Gobta!

06:35.100 --> 06:37.940
His aloof demeanor makes him
a subject of admiration to many!

06:38.020 --> 06:40.860
The genius, elite fighter!

06:41.150 --> 06:44.700
How did I end up in here?
Did someone sign me in?

06:44.950 --> 06:48.320
That Soka, she sure knows
how to overhype the crowd.

06:48.410 --> 06:51.120
Aloof? Genius? None of
that matches Gobta at all.

06:53.750 --> 06:56.370
Were you trying to say something, Raphael?

06:57.130 --> 06:59.250
And that's all for the warm-up acts.

06:59.340 --> 07:02.590
I now present you with our eighth
competitor, the star performer-

07:03.050 --> 07:06.550
The guardian angel of Tempest,
repelling all with his invulnerable defense;

07:06.880 --> 07:09.260
The savior of the High Orcs,

07:09.350 --> 07:12.470
Geld!

07:13.140 --> 07:15.980
Now we have all eight
competitors in the ring!

07:16.060 --> 07:18.730
Who's going to reign supreme?

07:18.810 --> 07:22.650
Let us first hear an opening
speech from Great Rimuru.

07:41.920 --> 07:43.000
Sensei!

07:43.090 --> 07:44.510
So cool!

07:46.340 --> 07:47.340
Fighters!

07:47.550 --> 07:51.510
If you win through today's matches
and win the final round tomorrow,

07:51.600 --> 07:54.770
I will grant you the glory of my nation.

07:54.850 --> 07:58.190
Be it the seat as the last member of
the Big Four or the right to challenge me,

07:58.270 --> 08:00.480
if you win this tournament,
it's all yours!

08:01.020 --> 08:02.820
I wish you all can give your best.

08:10.740 --> 08:12.830
Hero Masayuki got the number three!

08:12.910 --> 08:15.830
With this, all the matches has been set.

08:15.910 --> 08:18.000
Wh-What's this?!

08:18.250 --> 08:20.670
His first opponent is Jinrai, his friend.

08:20.750 --> 08:23.380
And the strong competitors
are all facing each others...

08:23.460 --> 08:25.880
This whole thing is all too good for him!

08:26.340 --> 08:29.680
<i>How am I supposed to gauge</i>
<i>his true strength with this?</i>

08:30.260 --> 08:33.430
<i>Did Masayuki manipulate</i>
<i>destiny or something somehow?</i>

08:33.930 --> 08:37.100
Now, let us start with our first match!

08:37.560 --> 08:39.730
How will their eternal rivalry end?

08:39.810 --> 08:42.650
Boyix versus Equix!

08:42.730 --> 08:45.360
Our fates have
intertwined for far too long.

08:45.440 --> 08:48.150
Prepare yourself, Equix!

08:48.240 --> 08:52.990
I am the one worthy to serve as
one of Great Rimuru's Big Four!

08:53.070 --> 08:58.080
You may enjoy your retirement
all holed up in the labyrinth, Boyix!

08:58.160 --> 09:00.580
Now, let's begin!

09:08.760 --> 09:15.100
I have the Extra skill Ultraspeed Regeneration,
granted to me by Great Rimuru!

09:16.470 --> 09:22.270
Your attacks are meaningless against
the Magical Interference he granted me!

09:22.350 --> 09:24.770
What intense clashes!

09:24.860 --> 09:27.900
This is the battle between
two A-ranked monsters!

09:30.150 --> 09:32.660
It's over!

09:36.080 --> 09:37.120
You fell for it.

09:37.200 --> 09:38.450
Wh-What?!

09:38.540 --> 09:42.330
Take this- Equine Spear Flail!

09:49.010 --> 09:50.630
Not enough!

09:51.760 --> 09:55.050
Eat this! Lightning Horn!

10:02.890 --> 10:04.060
Game!

10:04.440 --> 10:06.520
The winner is Boyix!

10:07.150 --> 10:11.030
I… won!

10:11.440 --> 10:14.070
Not for long. I'll win next time.

10:14.160 --> 10:19.080
Look! Although they have suffered so much
injures, their wounds have started to heal!

10:19.160 --> 10:21.290
This is the strength of A-ranked monsters!

10:21.500 --> 10:25.420
I believe they both will serve
as good master of the dungeon!

10:28.460 --> 10:30.670
Now, to the second match!

10:31.260 --> 10:32.260
Hero Masayuki versus-

10:32.340 --> 10:35.380
The winner is Hero Masayuki.

10:35.470 --> 10:39.100
Jinrai the Mad Wolf forfeit the match!

10:39.180 --> 10:41.390
Hero Masayuki wins by default!

10:41.470 --> 10:43.140
Wonderful!

10:43.230 --> 10:45.190
He won by default!

10:45.270 --> 10:47.310
He's so amazing!

10:47.860 --> 10:49.110
Unacceptable.

10:51.940 --> 10:54.570
Now, let's move on to the third match!

10:54.650 --> 10:58.370
Gaiye the Flowing Swordsman versus Gobta!

11:01.990 --> 11:05.710
Demon Lord! I am stronger
than the earlier Hero!

11:05.790 --> 11:08.500
If I win this tournament,
I'll have you fight me!

11:10.090 --> 11:11.050
<i>Huh?</i>

11:12.380 --> 11:16.970
Be it the Hero or the Demon Lord,
I'll make them bow down before me!

11:17.050 --> 11:19.720
What an unacceptable
attitude towards Great Rimuru…

11:19.800 --> 11:24.520
M-Mr. Diablo, you're the judge right now,
so let's have Gobta deal with him instead.

11:24.770 --> 11:26.690
Now, begin!

11:29.900 --> 11:32.730
The match has started with
Gaiye's sharp attacks!

11:32.820 --> 11:35.610
His title of "Flowing Swordsman"
is not just for show!

11:37.450 --> 11:38.450
It's over!

11:39.700 --> 11:43.080
What?! A peon like you
wear such a fine armory?!

11:44.370 --> 11:45.910
That's too fast!

11:46.000 --> 11:47.580
Heh! You're not getting away!

11:50.790 --> 11:53.340
Run, you pathetic little weakling!

11:54.710 --> 11:58.340
Is that man trying to make
Gobta his punching bag?

11:58.430 --> 11:59.970
That's disgusting.

12:00.050 --> 12:04.350
I wish he try a little harder,
and not just running away.

12:04.430 --> 12:07.140
But Gobta is being very observant.

12:07.390 --> 12:12.270
He wouldn't be able to dodge for so long unless
he could keep up with how he moved his weapon.

12:12.610 --> 12:13.610
Oh?

12:14.940 --> 12:16.280
Gobta!

12:17.150 --> 12:20.320
Show us your guts and beat that guy!

12:20.490 --> 12:24.950
If you win, I'll give you that latest
fishing rod you always wanted!

12:25.040 --> 12:27.080
Oh? For real?!

12:28.660 --> 12:31.250
Then I'll show you my trump card!

12:32.840 --> 12:35.670
Don't get too cocky with me, peon!

12:35.750 --> 12:36.920
Summon!

12:37.010 --> 12:38.840
Now, come on over!

12:39.590 --> 12:41.470
Heh! A summon?

12:41.550 --> 12:44.260
But a mere dark direwolf
is no match against me-

12:44.510 --> 12:45.180
Huh?

12:46.680 --> 12:47.390
Huh?

12:51.440 --> 12:52.650
Game!

12:53.110 --> 12:56.150
The winner is Gobta!

12:56.230 --> 13:00.200
What a brilliant attack that
knocks Gaiye out in just one hit!

13:02.070 --> 13:04.070
Huh? Why Ranga's here?

13:04.620 --> 13:10.080
Ranga must've sneaked into Gobta's summoning
because he wanted to join this so badly.

13:16.000 --> 13:18.090
The Colosseum is still
burning with excitement!

13:18.170 --> 13:22.050
Our next and fourth match is
between two of our strongest fighters!

13:22.130 --> 13:25.470
Lion Max versus Geld!

13:31.560 --> 13:34.150
Such a fierce offense and defense!

13:34.230 --> 13:36.730
Against Lion Mask's
numerous sharp attacks,

13:36.820 --> 13:39.860
Geld fights with his  invulnerable
defense and heavy blows!

13:39.940 --> 13:42.360
This is a fight nobody can
turn their eyes away from!

13:43.450 --> 13:45.490
Man, this is fun!

13:45.570 --> 13:49.580
You're taking my blows
like they're a passing breeze!

13:49.660 --> 13:52.750
Heh-heh, I am the one
who should be complaining.

13:55.750 --> 13:58.500
A clash of techniques!
A clash of power!

13:58.590 --> 14:00.590
Neither of them are backing down!

14:00.670 --> 14:02.130
W-Wow!

14:02.220 --> 14:04.510
I've never seen a match like this!

14:07.560 --> 14:10.020
Do your best, Lion Mask!

14:11.930 --> 14:15.560
You've done well to hold
out against me this long.

14:15.980 --> 14:17.190
You have my compliments.

14:17.270 --> 14:19.400
Heh-heh, it is an honor.

14:19.690 --> 14:22.280
But, let me ask you one thing.

14:22.570 --> 14:25.030
Why aren't you using any skills?

14:27.320 --> 14:30.290
Because you still have not
shown your true self to me.

14:35.420 --> 14:36.540
I see!

14:36.630 --> 14:41.130
So you were aiming for a win
by playing on the same field as me?

14:41.210 --> 14:42.800
Interesting!

14:43.590 --> 14:46.050
I can't show you my beast form,

14:46.140 --> 14:49.050
but I'll give respect to your guts
and show you some real moves!

14:56.770 --> 14:58.860
Lion Cannon Fist!

15:09.370 --> 15:12.790
W-Well… done…

15:16.460 --> 15:17.750
Game!

15:18.500 --> 15:21.090
The long intense battle
finally came to an end!

15:21.170 --> 15:24.340
The winner of this intense battle
is Lion Mask!

15:24.970 --> 15:26.970
You should be proud, Geld.

15:27.340 --> 15:32.350
You can still stand even after taking
my Lion Cannon Fist.

15:32.770 --> 15:37.900
Heh. I would love for us to fight
with full strength someday.

15:38.270 --> 15:39.480
So would I.

15:39.560 --> 15:42.650
I haven't had a fight
this fun in a while.

15:52.870 --> 15:58.210
Now we have our winners,
let us move on to the semifinals.

15:58.460 --> 16:02.590
The amount of injures and how fatigued the
competitors are will determine the winners.

16:02.840 --> 16:08.090
Now, our fifth match,
Masayuki the Hero versus Boyix!

16:08.180 --> 16:09.970
Yes, she is right.

16:10.050 --> 16:10.590
What?

16:11.010 --> 16:14.560
You did wonderful in your earlier match.

16:14.720 --> 16:15.560
Huh?

16:15.640 --> 16:17.480
Y-Yeah.

16:17.940 --> 16:19.940
But that makes it all the more a pity.

16:20.020 --> 16:23.980
With how you have used majority
of your power today,

16:24.070 --> 16:25.360
I'm likely gonna win.

16:25.570 --> 16:26.820
What?!

16:26.900 --> 16:30.070
But if you were in peak shape…

16:30.570 --> 16:33.910
If we were to fight in your
home ground at the dungeon…

16:34.160 --> 16:36.290
Whoa, whoa, you're kidding me…

16:36.700 --> 16:40.330
I'll be tackling the dungeon here after this.

16:40.620 --> 16:42.460
To where you'll be waiting.

16:42.710 --> 16:43.880
What do you say?

16:43.960 --> 16:48.510
How about we save this match for
when you'll face me in your peak shape?

16:56.600 --> 16:58.930
You're absolutely right.

16:59.020 --> 17:01.690
I defeated Equix by
only a razor-thin margin,

17:01.770 --> 17:03.650
and I have no strength
to spare right now.

17:06.030 --> 17:07.030
Very well!

17:07.110 --> 17:11.070
I'll trust your words and wait
for your arrival in the labyrinth.

17:13.280 --> 17:15.160
Forfeit! Boyix has forfeited!

17:15.240 --> 17:19.290
Boyix just gave the match
to Hero Masayuki!

17:19.460 --> 17:20.620
I knew it!

17:20.710 --> 17:25.380
He even give mercy to his opponent!
How merciful!

17:25.460 --> 17:27.590
Sir Masayuki! He's so wonderful!

17:27.670 --> 17:34.090
Masayuki! Masayuki!
Masayuki! Masayuki!

17:34.180 --> 17:37.390
Wait, wait. Why's everyone
acting like that makes any sense?

17:37.600 --> 17:40.850
Is this the work of a hero's
charisma or something?

17:49.740 --> 17:51.950
Hmm, unacceptable.

17:53.110 --> 17:56.240
We will now begin the
final match of the day!

17:56.740 --> 18:00.620
The masked beast who won
that fierce battle, Lion Mask!

18:00.700 --> 18:04.790
And the young warrior who grasped
victory with his quick wits, Gobta!

18:05.080 --> 18:08.710
Which one of them will
move on to the final tomorrow?

18:09.710 --> 18:11.550
There he is! Lion Mask!

18:11.630 --> 18:13.630
Show us another amazing match!

18:13.720 --> 18:15.390
Do your best too, Gobta!

18:15.470 --> 18:17.350
Don't just run this time, okay!

18:17.680 --> 18:21.140
If I win this, give me that new
fishing rod like you promised, okay!

18:21.230 --> 18:24.310
I heard this new one
got an improved fishing reel!

18:24.390 --> 18:26.310
You better win this, okay?

18:26.810 --> 18:29.230
Well, I bet Carrion will just win thi-

18:29.320 --> 18:32.240
I mean, Lion Mask will.

18:32.610 --> 18:36.990
I couldn't ask for a better person
to test out Masayuki's strength.

18:37.370 --> 18:39.540
Now, begin!

18:39.620 --> 18:42.330
I'm not the hobgoblin I usually am today!

18:46.630 --> 18:48.380
Don't make me laugh, kid.

18:48.460 --> 18:50.590
I won't be too mean to you,
so hurry up and forfeit-

18:50.670 --> 18:52.670
Ranga, you're up!

18:52.760 --> 18:54.300
Yes, at once!

18:57.010 --> 18:59.180
Tiger Talon!

19:00.470 --> 19:02.180
There! There! There!

19:04.230 --> 19:06.400
C'mon, just running again?

19:06.480 --> 19:07.860
Make it a real fight!

19:07.940 --> 19:09.820
This <i>is</i> a fight!

19:09.900 --> 19:10.940
With Ranga, that is!

19:16.740 --> 19:18.780
Elephant Stampede!

19:20.700 --> 19:23.790
Lion Mask is shooting down
a barrage of aura shots!

19:23.870 --> 19:26.830
Can Gobta and Ranga dodge all of this?!

19:28.420 --> 19:31.090
R-Ranga fled to outside the ring!

19:31.170 --> 19:31.920
What?!

19:32.000 --> 19:34.010
Got you! Take this!

19:36.260 --> 19:38.390
Weren't you out of the ring?!

19:40.050 --> 19:43.640
A resummon is not against the rule.

19:43.720 --> 19:46.600
Gobta thought of it this far?

19:47.770 --> 19:50.110
Ranga attacked on the opening!

19:50.190 --> 19:52.820
But Lion Mask dodged it as well!

19:52.900 --> 19:55.690
<i>I should've worried more of the wolf!</i>

19:55.900 --> 19:59.530
O-Oh! Lion Mask's face is exposed!

19:59.620 --> 20:02.700
Gobta's target was his mask all along!

20:02.780 --> 20:04.950
Now you can't use both of your hands!

20:05.120 --> 20:07.960
Eat this! Icicle Lance!

20:10.040 --> 20:11.590
Tch, you little sneak!

20:11.670 --> 20:14.420
Lion Mask's fighting while
desperately hiding his face!

20:14.500 --> 20:16.550
Now he can't do anything but defend!

20:16.630 --> 20:19.050
What a cowardly way to fight!

20:19.130 --> 20:20.890
Fight for real, you bastard!

20:20.970 --> 20:24.970
Shut up! In this world,
as long as you win, you're right!

20:25.180 --> 20:27.600
Great Rimuru said so himself!

20:27.980 --> 20:29.230
I can see that.

20:29.310 --> 20:31.190
Yeah, sounds like something he'd say.

20:32.480 --> 20:34.610
<i>Please, don't get me involved in this.</i>

20:35.530 --> 20:39.910
Okay, okay. I'll let you win.
You've outwitted me this time.

20:41.070 --> 20:43.370
I forfeit this match.

20:45.950 --> 20:46.830
Game!

20:46.910 --> 20:50.960
It's an upset! The table has
been flipped upside down!

20:51.040 --> 20:53.250
The winner is Gobta!

20:53.340 --> 20:55.090
I did it!

20:56.050 --> 20:59.010
That warps up today's matches!

21:01.760 --> 21:04.430
Please look forward for
tomorrow's match!

21:04.510 --> 21:08.770
A final between Masayuki the Hero
and the Big Four candidate Gobta!

21:09.060 --> 21:13.020
I have been your host, Soka!

21:22.570 --> 21:24.160
That was amazing!

21:24.240 --> 21:27.870
Sir Masayuki was so stunning
even when he was just standing!

21:27.950 --> 21:30.370
I like Lion Mask more.

21:30.460 --> 21:31.670
I like Geld!

21:31.750 --> 21:34.080
Those two were really awesome!

21:35.790 --> 21:37.340
Sir Lion Mask!

21:38.510 --> 21:41.050
Looks like they saw
just how cool I am.

21:41.430 --> 21:43.180
They got good eyes.

21:43.260 --> 21:46.390
Don't be silly! How can you be "cool"
when you can't even win the tournament?

21:54.190 --> 21:56.820
Everyone was so excited
even after the matches are over.

21:56.900 --> 22:01.610
And the stores are brimming
with customers, racking a big profit!

22:01.700 --> 22:03.860
The kids looked like they had fun, too.

22:03.950 --> 22:06.580
Seems like Day Two wrapped up nicely.

22:07.030 --> 22:12.660
But who would've thought the one
to face Masayuki in the final be Gobta.

22:13.420 --> 22:17.670
If you ask me, I think that
Gobta kid has some potential.

22:17.880 --> 22:19.550
Huh? What do you mean?

22:20.710 --> 22:24.970
Meaning, maybe
Masayuki will lose tomorrow.

22:28.310 --> 22:29.310
Great Rimuru?

22:29.470 --> 22:32.930
I mean, I'm aware he
has a lot of good sense.

22:33.020 --> 22:37.150
Maybe he can tap into some kind of
hidden strength by fighting the Hero.

22:37.900 --> 22:41.360
But still… It's Gobta.

22:44.450 --> 22:47.910
<i>Did Raphael wanted to say something again?</i>

22:50.580 --> 22:51.870
Did you wait long?

24:26.260 --> 24:28.970
Next time, "The Battle with the Hero."
